%% Phase 15 — one publish, from "ask" to "read back".
%% An item is called published only on the PUBLISHED branch. See docs/MARKETING.md.

sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant P as Page or chat
    participant E as ToolExecutor
    participant S as MarketingService
    participant A as Approval (PostgreSQL)
    participant J as Execution journal
    participant F as Facebook Page

    U->>P: Publish this item
    P->>E: marketing.publish.prepare (a read)
    E->>S: preparePublish
    S->>F: list the Pages this connection may post to
    S-->>P: publishParams — the saved text, the Page
    P->>A: create approval, bound by hash to those parameters
    P-->>U: the exact text and Page. Nothing has been sent.

    U->>A: approve (one conditional UPDATE)
    P->>E: marketing.content.publish, naming that approval
    E->>J: begin execution, keyed by the approval
    E->>A: consume the approval WITH the execution claim
    E->>S: publish
    S->>S: again — still ready? saved text = approved text? Page still listed, same name?
    S->>S: claimForPublish (one conditional UPDATE)

    alt an earlier attempt was never confirmed, and its post is found
        S->>F: read that post by id, then look for the exact text
        F-->>S: found
        S-->>P: ALREADY_PUBLISHED — nothing new sent
    else nothing to reconcile
        S->>F: POST the post
        alt accepted and read back
            F-->>S: post id
            S->>F: read the post back by its id
            F-->>S: the post, with the text that was sent
            S->>S: record PUBLISHED · VERIFIED
            S-->>P: PUBLISHED
        else accepted, cannot be read back
            S->>S: leave unpublished, UNCONFIRMED, keep the post id
            S-->>P: UNCONFIRMED — outcome not known
        else refused
            F-->>S: refusal
            S-->>P: FAILED — nothing was published
        else the answer never arrives
            S->>S: leave unpublished, UNCONFIRMED
            S-->>P: UNCONFIRMED — outcome not known
        end
    end
